extraction_notes: "NPC-HEADED: the stat block is titled ''Dragon-Cat NPC and Optional Player Character'' (printed 100), so it is playable as an option; the Player Character Note says any Dragon-Cat allowed as a player character is likely young and inexperienced, first or second level - recorded in side_effects and GM Notes, not enforced. xp_table is the batch''s reading of printed 157. THE BOOK PRINTS NO SKILLS, NO O.C.C., NO EQUIPMENT AND NO MONEY for the Dragon-Cat, and none is invented; it also says nothing either way about taking an O.C.C., so no occ_restrictions is stated (it never uses technology and cannot speak, which the restrictions record). men_of_arms: false because it is a race; the pool is mdc_base (M.D.C.: 4D6x10 + P.E., +3D6 per level). PROWL 70%, CLIMB 65%, SWIM 50%, GYMNASTICS 70% and TRACK BY SMELL 46% are printed as fixed Natural Abilities, not R.C.C. skills, so they are natural_abilities (display) rather than skill rows - taking them as catalog skills would add per-level growth and the Gymnastics skill''s own bonuses, neither of which the book grants. I.S.P. is printed ''1D6x10+10 per level'' (render of printed 101 confirms); read as 1D6x10 at first level plus 10 per level, the Master Psychic pattern and the dog-boy/psycho-stalker precedent - the other reading (1D6x10+10 rolled every level) is noted here. The psionic tier is ''the equivalent of a Master Psychic with limited abilities'', stored as type master; nine named powers plus one Physical, one Sensitive and two Healing of choice (powers_starting_groups). ''Impervious to Cold'' is the printed name and matches its own catalog row (distinct from Resist Cold). Magic: nine innate spells granted by name with spells_starting 0; ''equal to a 3rd level Ley Line Walker regardless of actual level'' is not expressible and is in special_abilities. ''+1 to save vs magic'' stored as saves.spell_magic. Five attacks per melee stored as combat.attacks_base (physical or psionic; two if by magic, prose). The rider-bond bonuses (+20% Exotic Horsemanship, +1 attack, +2 initiative, +1 strike, +1 parry, +6 M.D. charging) belong to the RIDER and are conditional, so they are prose in special_abilities, not bonuses. Horror Factor 12 stored in horror_factor. Average level (NPC) 1D4+3 is a population fact, not stored. Lifespan 200-300 years, size 8-10 ft tall / 15-20 ft long, weight 1200-1800 lbs are prose. Cache digit faults 4D6xlO, 2D4xlO, 3D6xlO, !D6xlO read as x10 per the brief and confirmed on the render."
---

## Lore

The Dragon-Cat looks like a monstrous six-legged hunting cat crossed with a dinosaur, ten feet tall with steel-rending claws and a scaly mega-damage hide. It is no dumb animal but an intelligent creature of magic, kin in spirit to the sphinx and the dragon, that wields innate spells and psionics and speaks only by telepathy. Most hold to a code much like a Cyber-Knight''s - life, freedom, honesty, loyalty and fair play - and many volunteer as mounts and allies for kindred spirits such as Mystical Indian Warriors, Wilderness Scouts, Cyber-Knights, Simvan, Psi-Druids and Psi-Warriors. Fewer than a thousand are thought to live in North America, mostly in the Magic Zone, the New West and the Canadian Northwest.

## GM Notes

Headed "Dragon-Cat NPC and Optional Player Character" (printed 100): playable as an option. The book''s Player Character Note says a played Dragon-Cat is young and inexperienced, first or second level, naive and curious like a dragon hatchling, never uses technology, and prefers wandering the wilderness to towns.

The book gives it no skills, O.C.C., equipment or money. Its spells always work at 3rd level Ley Line Walker strength. The rider-bond bonuses go on the bonded rider''s sheet, not the cat''s.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-cat');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-cat';

